# Cloudflare Pages routing. First-match-wins; static files take precedence.
#
# Rules Cloudflare enforces (both silently ignored before we knew):
#  (a) status must be one of 200/301/302/303/307/308 — anything else is dropped.
#  (b) a 200-rewrite whose target re-matches its source (a /X/* -> /X/index.html
#      loop) is treated as infinite and IGNORED — only the single root SPA
#      fallback (/* -> /index.html) is honoured.

# NO TRAILING SLASHES — enforce via 301, not convention. Applies to every path
# segment; `:splat` captures the rest of the URL after the leading `/`.
# The trailing-slash form is always the pre-image, the clean form is the target.
/*/                       /:splat                301

# Legacy www → apex (Cloudflare handles this at the DNS/proxy layer for many
# setups; kept here as a belt-and-suspenders redirect for any request that does
# reach Pages with the www host). No-op if the DNS layer already handles it.

# SPA fallback — every non-prerendered URL falls through to the home index.html
# and the SPA takes over. main.tsx strips the fallback's SEO tags before mount
# so react-helmet-async writes fresh from the visited page's <SEO> component.
/*                        /index.html            200
